- **Main user flows:**
  - Build library (left sidebar): add Sensors / Lenses via `From datasheet link` (paste URL → review pre-filled form → confirm) or `Add manually`; remove entries.
  - Compare cameras (main column): 1–4 camera panels, each = sensor dropdown + lens dropdown + working-distance slider; each renders 3D FOV cone + numeric readout (FOV, mm/pixel, compatibility) at shared 1:1 scale.
  - Review summaries: to-scale 2D sensor-size overlay (auto-fed from sensors in play) + table of Camera-1 sensor vs. all lenses in play (FOV, compatibility flags, spatial resolution).
  - Persist/share: localStorage autosave + Export/Import JSON; no login.
- **Data:**
  - 4 seed sensors (Sony IMX264, IMX178, IMX267, IMX392) + 4 seed lenses (Computar V1226-MPZ, Commonlands CIL532/CIL525/CIL060), hand-curated from Sony flyers + vendor pages, bundled as static JSON with provenance URLs.
  - User data: manual + datasheet-imported entries, stored only in browser localStorage; no server DB.
- **Frontend (plain language):**
  - Single-page app, sidebar-library + main-comparison layout.
  - Pieces: sensor/lens entry forms, datasheet-import form, side-by-side 3D camera panels, 2D sensor-size chart, comparison table, FOV numbers readout. 2D = scaled rectangles; 3D = orbitable camera frustum via three.js.
  - Pure calculation module for FOV/magnification/compatibility/resolution with unit tests.
- **Backend (plain language):**
  - One endpoint only: `POST /api/extract-datasheet {url, kind}` → returns structured sensor/lens fields + found/not-found per field.
  - Server fetches URL, extracts PDF/HTML text, asks Claude to map to data model; rate-limited, stateless, stores nothing. Local dev proxies `/api/*` to a small Node stand-in.
- **Top 3 gaps vs. better version:**
  - No requirement-driven selection: can't input "need X mm FOV at Y mm WD to see Z mm feature" and get ranked recommendations; user must brute-force combos.
  - Tiny static catalog, no search/filter: 8 seeds, no vendor database, parametric filtering, or sorting by FOV/resolution/price/availability.
  - No application context: no industry presets (UAV, embedded, inspection), mount/interface guidance, lighting/exposure, distortion/DoF, or cost/availability — the Reddit pain points.

